{
  "schema": 1,
  "feature": "108-roadmap-loop",
  "oracle": "G-L1",
  "comparison": {
    "nextCalls": "Each `next` call is compared on outcome, step, row, reason (exact strings or null), and on `skips` when the expected entry has it (map of not-started row id -> skip reason; must be equal as a map). `annotations` are for humans and are not compared.",
    "otherActions": "status/render/render --check calls are compared on the keys present in the expected entry.",
    "final": "Final facts are checked after the last call of the scenario.",
    "stepConvention": "`step` is one of pick|gate|merge|render|cleanup when the output concerns one of those steps (acted, gate denies, merge denies, a stop inside S8), else null (perform, idle, lease-held, stops at step start, blocked rows, loop denies). This convention is an assumption (IC-001 names `step` values only for `acted`).",
    "rowConvention": "`row` is the seed row id the output concerns, null for idle, stops at step start and lease-held."
  },
